# Brewfile — system-level dependencies for Rando.id development.
#
# Install or sync with:
#   brew bundle install
#
# Verify what's missing without installing:
#   brew bundle check
#
# `rando doctor` runs `brew bundle check` automatically when a Brewfile
# is present, and silences entries it can detect installed via other
# routes (npm, .dmg, 1Password desktop app, etc. — see brew.ts).

# ── Core dev toolchain ────────────────────────────────────────────────
brew "gh"               # GitHub CLI — used by `rando issues` orchestrators + `rando secrets push`
brew "pnpm"             # workspace tooling
brew "node@22"          # Node 22+ required by the CLI bin shebang
brew "1password-cli"    # `op` — secret resolution via `rando secrets` (sync, set, push)

# ── Container runtime — pick whichever you prefer ─────────────────────
# OrbStack is the lighter-weight default. Swap for `cask "docker"` if
# you prefer Docker Desktop. Either provides the `docker` CLI that
# `rando dev` (Postgres + tunnel) needs. The tunnel + Postgres both
# run inside Docker, so `cloudflared` and `postgresql` aren't needed
# on the host directly.
cask "orbstack"

# ── Optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uncomment if you actually use the corresponding `rando` commands.
# brew "postgresql@16"  # pg_dump / pg_restore for `rando db copy` (host-side DB dump/restore)
# brew "cloudflared"    # only if you run cloudflared on the host instead of in Docker
